<urn:atm:triage:finding/QA-AO2-R4-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "QA-AO2-R4-001" ;
  triage:title "just validate fails — 5 real-time-sleep-in-test-scope violations now caught by FTQ-003's widened lint (tokio::time::sleep coverage)" ;
  triage:description "FTQ-003 (already fixed and closed) widened .just/check_fixed_sleep_hygiene.py's SLEEP_RE to also match tokio::time::sleep, not just std::thread::sleep. That widened lint now correctly fails `just validate` because it found 5 real, pre-existing/unremediated real-time-sleep-in-test-scope call sites in this phase's touched files, none of which are in lint-config.toml's allowed_paths and none of which have a waiver filed. This blocks the phase gate per docs/plans/phase-ao2/readiness.md's requirement that `just validate` be green. For each, the fix is: convert the enclosing test to `#[tokio::test(start_paused = true)]` and use `tokio::time::advance(Duration::from_millis(...))` instead of a real `tokio::time::sleep(...)`, matching the exact pattern already used to fix FTQ-002 in peer_connection_pool.rs (a different test in that same file, already fixed and closed). Note: crates/atm-http-runtime/src/message_handler.rs:1760 (originally listed as occurrence #2) is already fixed as part of FTQ-004 and therefore not included in this sweep." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ao2" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-26T08:00:43Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AO2.15 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-26T07:58:38Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/QA-AO2-R4-001/QA-AO2-R4-001-occ-1> ;
